ef 1078 #edb/ref 17592186511246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511405 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a8dc6b69-1ae0-561f-a21b-1f490d47e054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186510976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511433 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186511048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511439 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7c15a59-5adc-5127-8074-bf8ca6a5dc2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511458 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511458 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511458 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0614088a-4b37-5f45-a256-f7dd1a417f0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511458 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511470 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511470 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511470 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "223797a4-3fdc-5efb-a9f2-b733398cd415" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511470 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & -{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ -{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,0),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,0)=(-1)\\cdot 1-{0}^{2}=-1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511486 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511486 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80945" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511486 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511486 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{″}(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511486 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y) & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511545 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511545 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511545 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511545 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{″}(1,\\pi )$ for the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511545 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511545 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
